{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Arur (cursed).</b> Just as in 'baruch' (blessed) it is an expression of abundance and success, so in 'arur' it is an expression of deficiency and loss. And so Onkelos translated in the language of tzara'at: 'ממארת' — 'a withholding of lack.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The final Aramaic phrase לשון צרעת ממארת סגירת מחסרא appears textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. The word ממארת is Onkelos's rendering of תמרור in Jer 6:7 (related to tzara'at), and סגירת מחסרא means 'a withholding/blocked state of lacking.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:31.583987589Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}